  "title": "Unusual Sessions",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "2309a038-1167-477e-b71f-73d81fd57159",
      "question": "Using the first half of 2025 as the baseline, which 10 sessions from July 1, 2025 through January 30, 2026 were the most unusual among the 1,000 most liquid US stocks, and which features made each one unusual? Anomaly scores are neither forecasts nor explanations.",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-07T15:22:10.782243Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-07T15:23:01.457278Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**BMNR on July 7, 2025 was the most unusual stock-session**, with an anomaly score of **2,450.47**. Its largest observed deviations were in five-day adjusted return and 20-day realized volatility. [1]\n\nThe ranking below uses **January–June 2025 as the baseline** and scores **July 1, 2025–January 30, 2026** in the 1,000-most-liquid-stock universe; the scan covered 991 assets. All feature values are **robust z-scores against the baseline**, not returns or percentages. Positive values indicate above-baseline readings; negative values indicate below-baseline readings. [1]\n\n| Rank | Ticker / session | Anomaly score | Features characterizing the unusual session |\n| --- | --- | ---: | --- |\n| 1 | BMNR · 2025-07-07 | 2,450.47 | Five-day return **+480.35**; 20-day volatility **+100.23**; one-day return −3.32; log-volume deviation +1.44. [1] |\n| 2 | DGNX · 2025-08-01 | 438.06 | One-day return **+359.72**; five-day return **+152.80**; 20-day volatility **+108.88**; log-volume deviation −2.20. [1] |\n| 3 | ABVX · 2025-07-23 | 277.15 | One-day return **+283.58**; five-day return **+117.57**; 20-day volatility **+85.20**; log-volume deviation +4.63. [1] |\n| 4 | BYND · 2025-10-23 | 82.29 | Five-day return **+87.08** and 20-day volatility **+30.31**, alongside one-day return **−10.28**; log-volume deviation +1.32. [1] |\n| 5 | DGNX · 2025-08-04 | 75.45 | Five-day return **+134.44**; 20-day volatility **+108.90**; one-day return −2.79; log-volume deviation −2.15. [1] |\n| 6 | DGNX · 2025-08-05 | 67.29 | Five-day return **+130.87**; 20-day volatility **+108.96**; one-day return −1.94; log-volume deviation −1.74. [1] |\n| 7 | BYND · 2025-10-22 | 66.03 | Five-day return **+85.07**; 20-day volatility **+30.04**; one-day return −1.80; log-volume deviation +1.92. [1] |\n| 8 | BMNR · 2025-07-14 | 64.45 | 20-day volatility **+100.98**, alongside five-day return **−12.19**; one-day return +0.59; log-volume deviation +1.07. [1] |\n| 9 | ABVX · 2025-07-29 | 63.79 | Five-day return **+118.43**; 20-day volatility **+85.30**; one-day return +2.38; log-volume deviation +0.79. [1] |\n| 10 | BMNR · 2025-07-15 | 62.49 | 20-day volatility **+100.90**, alongside five-day return **−12.89**; one-day return −1.77; log-volume deviation +0.70. [1] |\n\nThese are **stock-session rankings**, so tickers can appear more than once. The feature deviations describe unusual observed combinations—not formal contributions to the anomaly score, forecasts, probabilities, or causal explanations. [1]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market anomaly scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:609701e1e738f91b9ed18c682542ed1706a354b7b248bab0384968eb66d5d09c`",
